WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.870
- Doctor, when the CDC
Director, Robert Redfield,

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:05.550
says these new guidelines
are meant to facilitate

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.000
the opening of schools around the country,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.280
not keep them closed.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.930
Based on your reading
of these new guidelines,

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.023
do you think they accomplish that goal?

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.470
- Well Wolf, they sound
different from the guidelines

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.820
that were released before.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.150
And I kept on thinking, what
is it that's so different?

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.370
And what's different is the tone,

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.320
because what I'm used
to seeing from the CDC

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.670
is leading with the science and the facts.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.650
And these guidelines sound like
they're cherry picking data

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.100
to make a specific policy point.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.300
And that's really concerning,
because what we need

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.570
from the CDC is not a
justification of why children

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.403
should be in school.

00:00:42.403 --> 00:00:44.440
We all know that, we all want that.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.370
But we want the CDC to lay out,

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.920
what are the criteria
that we need to meet?

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.947
For example, we need to test
positivity less than 5%,

00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:54.670
a consistent, 14 day decline
in the number of cases.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.580
Something like that.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.460
And also, here's a
checklist of what schools

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.330
have to do in order for schools,

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.690
for them to reopen safely, in person.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.840
That's not what the CDC
really has laid out.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.710
And I really worry, if we can't trust

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.260
that what comes out from
them is based on science

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.982
and not politics, then who can we trust?

00:01:10.982 --> 00:01:13.500
- Yeah, that's a real serious
potential problem out there.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.410
Sal, you just had an excellent interview

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.560
with Dr. Anthony Fauci, yourself,

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.410
and you asked him about bringing teachers

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.010
and the students back to school.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.093
Let me play this clip. Listen to this.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:27.290
- When you talk about forcing teachers

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.060
to come back to school, you
better be careful about that,

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:35.060
and make sure you pay attention
to A, keeping them safe,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.853
and key, keeping them healthy.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.110
- Sal, I want you to elaborate
a little bit on that for us.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.843
What are some of the best
practices that Dr. Fauci outlined?

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.260
- Yeah well, first of all,
just to completely agree

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.430
with what was just said.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.500
What I think, we're talking
to school district leaders

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.420
around the country, and
what they're craving

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.490
is just very clear guidelines.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:58.520
What is the per capita
incidence rate, and for each

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.560
of those levels, what is
the appropriate action?

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.110
And there's good groups, like
the Harvard Global Health

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.450
Initiative Institute, that have been

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.200
doing very clear guidelines.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.680
And Dr. Fauci did seem to say
that those types of guidelines

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.250
are what folks could index on.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.490
And the timing is super important,

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.140
'cause we're only four to six weeks away

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.230
from school starting, and school leaders

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.760
really even haven't had a chance to think

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.490
about how the instruction's
going to happen,

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.280
'cause they don't know how
it's going to be structured.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.790
In terms of what we just
heard from the statement

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.760
about teachers, I did
ask him very directly,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.750
should teachers be forced to go back?

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.590
And he seemed pretty
empathetic with the situation,

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.850
especially for older teachers,

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.340
teachers who might have some
other health circumstances,

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.030
that they shouldn't be
forced to go back to school.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:42.820
We talked about social
distancing, but once again,

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.040
it would be valuable to
get very clear guidelines

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.280
of what's good and what is not.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.610
And also, there's interesting ideas

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.120
of maybe leveraging outdoor classrooms.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.620
There's a South Korean study talking

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.060
about over 10 years old,
versus under 10 years old.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.880
What can we do with say, kindergarteners

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.080
or first graders, outdoors?

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.220
Some type of clear
guidance along those lines

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.330
would be super valuable.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.640
- You're absolutely right.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.630
Dr. Wen, even as the white house pushes

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.060
a complete return to schools, a key member

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.100
of the corona virus task
force, Dr. Deborah Birx,

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.730
is cautioning that it's unclear
how rapidly young children,

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:19.890
even under the age of 10,
can transmit the virus.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.500
So we know this one study
that Sal was referring to,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.610
in South Korea, said that children over 10

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.500
transmit the virus as
quickly and as thoroughly

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.620
as adults do.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.790
What additional evidence
would you like to see

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.683
on that critically important front?

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.620
- Yeah, so that particular
study from South Korea,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.600
it actually only looked
at symptomatic people.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.300
So we don't know about
asymptomatic transmission,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.730
and since 40%, or even more,
of cases are transmitted

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.340
by people without symptoms,
we really don't know

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.750
whether asymptomatic
children, young children,

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.680
can transmit just as
much as older people too.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.520
I think also, when you look at
the studies done of children,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.320
they have all been in countries
where the transmission

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.410
rate is really low, and
so we really have no idea

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.080
what it's going to look like in the US,

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.100
if kids are going back in places

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.630
where there are active surges.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.240
And I'm afraid that this looks like

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.680
an uncontrolled environment,
where our children,

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:16.470
and our teachers, and their
families, are guinea pigs.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.460
- You know Sal, in your interview,

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.900
Dr. Fauci also spoke about
the potential downsides

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.290
of relying on face shields in schools,

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:27.460
rather than requiring students
and teachers to wear masks.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.473
I wanna play this clip, watch this.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.780
- My staff just brought this in. (laughs)

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.613
- There you go.

00:04:35.613 --> 00:04:37.460
- This was a great-
- That's exactly what, yeah.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.067
- Like that? Yeah.

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:40.740
- Good look.
- So this is good, yeah.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.730
This is good for droplets,
'cause it'll block it.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:47.140
The only trouble is if you
have any degree of aerosol,

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.850
what's happens, is that all of this,

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.930
see, it can go right in like that.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.720
That's the problem, you see?

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.200
So these are good for droplets,

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.250
but you have to be careful
if there's a degree

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.330
of aerosolization.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.040
- So if you wear a face shield, Sal,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.880
you should also still wear a mask,

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.430
I guess that's what he's suggesting.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.270
But for younger children, especially,

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.750
it would be helpful to
see the teachers face.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.820
If face shields aren't very protective

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.920
in a classroom setting, and
everyone has to wear a mask,

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.250
which they clearly do,
what impact is all this

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.093
going to have on the
critical issue of learning?

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.460
- It's going to have a huge impact.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.570
Just from the school closures
that have already occurred,

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:26.910
over the spring, a lot
of researchers think

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.440
it's going to be as much
as a year of learning loss.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.840
'Cause not only were kids not learning,

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.110
they were also forgetting,
they were atrophying.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.780
And basically the
conversation with Dr. Fauci,

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.830
even if one of either the
Moderna, or one of the vaccines

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.910
become successful, and we're
able to start deploying

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.940
them in January, you're
still not going to get

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.060
to herd immunity, get them all deployed,

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.650
until several months later.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.260
It's a major public
health issue to be able

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.260
to get hundreds of
millions of vaccines out.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.640
And so this is going to
be this entire school year

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:58.640
in some form of socially-distanced
or hybrid learning.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.620
And so it's going to be a
really, really tough year.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.120
And the biggest fear is it's
going to drive more inequity.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.800
All of our children, my children, I think,

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.590
are just going to be fine,
but there's a lot of kids

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.780
who don't have the supports,
who don't have the access,

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.430
and they're also going
to be going to schools

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.860
that might not have the resources

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.900
to be able to provide them adequately.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.550
So it's going to be a tough year.

